ed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in vertex-index order."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Storage is compressed sparse rows: the members of every hyperedge in one array, and for every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex its incidence numbers and, beside them, its hyperedge positions, in rows of shared"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pools. "},{"code":"memberIndices","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"incidentHyperedges(ofIndex:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" are stored "},{"code":"ArraySlice<Int>","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" rows"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"read without hashing, and the hypergraph makes a constant number of allocations however many"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertices it has. Every vertex-space read hashes its vertex once; index-space reads and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"Hypergraphs","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" algorithms hash none."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Hyperedges can be appended but not removed. Equality ignores the order of the vertices and of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the hyperedges."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Maps from the vertices and the hyperedges to values can be attached (","type":"text"},{"code":"PropertyGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"): a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertex map is read by vertex index or by vertex, an edge map by hyperedge position.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/PropertyGraph":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"PropertyGraph"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/PropertyGraph","url":"\/documentation\/gr